{#
calendar/_ics_subscribe.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Subscribe to a calendar published at an address.

A hand-written form rather than a Symfony one, for the reason
calendar/_subscribe.html.twig gives and one more of its own: the Integration
behind this is created by IcsFeedConnector, not bound by the form, because the
name has to be made unique against the connections the user already has before
an entity can carry it. A form type mapping a field it must then overwrite is
worse than no form type.

Two fields and one warning. The warning is the point of the intro paragraph:
for a published calendar the address IS the credential — Google and Outlook
both call theirs a secret address — so pasting one into a shared screen is the
same act as pasting a password, and nothing on screen would otherwise say so.

There is no "which calendars?" step. A feed is one calendar, so the connect
answers with the settings list rather than with a tick-box list of one; see
CalendarSubscriber::subscribeAll().

Wrapped in the modal frame directly rather than through
_partials/_modal_form.html.twig, which needs a FormView it does not have. The
frame is what Turbo swaps into; a response without it leaves the dialog on its
spinner.

Variables:
  error  string|null  why the address was refused, already written for a person
  url    string       what was submitted, so a refused address comes back
                      editable rather than making the user paste it again
#}
{% extends '_layout/app.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
<turbo-frame id="modal">
    <template data-ui--modal-frame-title>{{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.title'|trans }}</template>

    <form method="post"
          action="{{ path('app_calendar_ics_subscribe') }}"
          data-turbo-frame="modal"
          class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('calendar-ics-subscribe') }}">

        <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 px-6 pb-6 space-y-4 overflow-y-auto">
            <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
                {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.intro'|trans }}
            </p>

            {% if error is not null %}
                <div role="alert" class="flex items-start gap-2.5 rounded-lg alert-danger px-3.5 py-3 text-sm text-danger">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation mt-0.5 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <p class="leading-snug">{{ error }}</p>
                </div>
            {% endif %}

            <div class="space-y-1.5">
                <label for="ics-url" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                    {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.address'|trans }}
                </label>
                {# type="url" is deliberately NOT used: the browser's own
                   validation rejects webcal:// outright, and webcal:// is what
                   every "Subscribe" button copies to the clipboard.
                   IcsUrlNormaliser rewrites it server-side. #}
                <input type="text"
                       id="ics-url"
                       name="url"
                       value="{{ url }}"
                       required
                       autocomplete="off"
                       spellcheck="false"
                       placeholder="https://example.com/holidays.ics"
                       class="w-full h-9 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                              focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">
                <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                    {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.address_help'|trans }}
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-1.5">
                <label for="ics-name" class="block text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
                    {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.name'|trans }}
                </label>
                <input type="text"
                       id="ics-name"
                       name="name"
                       autocomplete="off"
                       class="w-full h-9 px-3 rounded-lg text-sm bg-field border border-field text-ink
                              focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent">
                <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                    {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.name_help'|trans }}
                </p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint leading-snug">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                {{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.read_only_note'|trans }}
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2 px-6 pb-6 pt-3 shrink-0">
            <button type="button"
                    data-action="click->ui--modal#close"
                    class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium
                           text-ink-soft bg-field border border-field hover:bg-hover
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'form.cancel'|trans }}</button>

            <button type="submit"
                    class="inline-flex items-center justify-center h-8 px-3.5 rounded-lg text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink
                           bg-accent hover:bg-accent-strong active:bg-blue-800
                           focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent focus-visible:ring-offset-1
                           transition-colors duration-100">{{ 'calendar.ics.subscribe.submit'|trans }}</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</turbo-frame>
{% endblock %}
